<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Green Standard Army</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Green Standard Army was the body of mainly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-chinese">Han Chinese</a> troops maintained by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a> alongside the Manchu-led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eight-banners">Eight Banners</a>. It was used largely for garrison and policing duties across the provinces. Its declining effectiveness in the nineteenth century contributed to the Qing reliance on new regional armies during major rebellions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/green-standard-army.jpg" alt="Green Standard Army" width="320" height="206" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Green_Standard_Army.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
